// Star Exploration (GDD, section 11): the resource mode, a journey through the 88 constellations of the sky
// in path order: the Boreal ones (center above +20 degrees of declination), the Equatorial ones (the middle
// band, with the 12 of the zodiac) and the Austral ones (center below -25 degrees). Each constellation is a
// floor. The journey starts over on day 1 of every month, and every month one of the three "explorations"
// (in rotation) brings its challenges; the "reward" of each constellation is always the same, paid by the
// first victory of the month (Core/Progression/Exploration.cs). Fights cost no Mana.
// "influence" is the constellation's mechanic, the same in the three explorations: rules that last the whole
// fight, each a passive (the same kinds as Data/summons, with value and effects) put on every unit of its
// "side": Foes (every enemy), Guardian (only the boss), Allies (the player's team) or Everyone. Effects aim
// from the point of view of whoever holds the rule. The written explanation, with how to beat it, is in the
// texts ("exploration.influence.<constellation id>"); the numbers are written by the game from the rules.
// "challenges" has one entry per exploration, in their order: the waves, with the guardian in the last one.
// A summon with "guardian": true is the boss of the fight: awakened, all skills at max level and boss HP
// (Core/Battle/BattleFactory.cs), so its skills are the challenge; a unique boss of Data/enemies.json is
// already a boss. "scale" (in the challenge) fine-tunes it over the constellation's strength.
// "stars", "level" and "scale" are the strength of every enemy, the same all year. "chart" is where the orb
// sits on its band's map, in points of a "chartWidth"-wide map: the projection of the real sky (polar for the
// Boreal and Austral bands, a strip for the Equatorial one), spread just enough for orbs not to touch. "ra"
// (hours) and "dec" (degrees) are the real center of the constellation. "icon" is in Assets/Icons (without
// the file, the map shows a star).
